{"name":"Mudskipper","hex":"#897a69","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mudskipper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various gobies of the subfamily Oxudercinae that are able to survive out of water by breathing through their skins and having strong pectoral fins that act as simple legs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mudskipper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mudskipper","blocks":[{"text":"Mudskippers are any of the 25 extant species of amphibious fish from the subfamily Oxudercinae of the goby family Oxudercidae. They are known for their unusual body shapes, preferences for semiaquatic habitats, limited terrestrial locomotion and jumping, and the ability to survive prolonged periods of time both in and out of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/GambianMudskippers.jpg/330px-GambianMudskippers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mudskipper","wikidata":"Q828079"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Periophthalmus_gracilis.jpg/330px-Periophthalmus_gracilis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Periophthalmus_gracilis.jpg/330px-Periophthalmus_gracilis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Periophthalmus gracilis (from Malaysia to northern Australia)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APeriophthalmus_gracilis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Schlammspringer_Periophthalmus_sp.jpg/500px-Schlammspringer_Periophthalmus_sp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Schlammspringer_Periophthalmus_sp.jpg/1280px-Schlammspringer_Periophthalmus_sp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa